I had exactly the same problem. The game would abruptly disapear with
a dramatic loud and abrupt click from my monitor as it changed modes.
I E-mailed the address given in the README.PC file for bugs & was ad-
vised back that this was a known bug & corrected executables had been 
posted.

Sure enough, the new version works great. My nethack.exe is 992,236K &
dated 8/4/93.

A couple of other Windows notes:

1) If you can, use DOS 6. The latest EMM386 (v4.45) can allocate EMS with-
out needing the amount specified in config.sys. This means you can use
NOEMS in the command line. With DOS 5, try Frame=None to get back the 64k
EMS page frame & increase the amount of upper memory available.

2) A poorly documented DOS 6 EMM386 command line parameter allows you to 
set the amount of EMS memory the DPMI manager will make available to apps
even with the NOEMS switch. I use NOEMS 4096 which speeds up the game 
tremendously over just the straight NOEMS setting.

3) Somewhere around 5 Meg is indeed the minimum. My laptop with 6 Meg
cannot run Nethack under Windows without completely turning off 
Smartdrive. (I should note I have only a two meg swap file due to my
tiny hard drive, so this may not limit everyone.)

